    {
      "text": "Place yuca into a large pot; add water to cover. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to medium-low. Cover and simmer until yuca can be pierced easily with a fork, 20 to 30 minutes. Drain and allow to steam for several minutes until cool enough to handle.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Di5JVb2sv1aKKG168TrdkxbMcXI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/RM-165419-yuca-french-fries-ddmfs-step2-3x4-13180-1c60b08aeb4747458f179c5e3064f8b9.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/165419/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cut yuca into French fry-sized sticks, discarding fibrous core.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/MyNIlBtWXmChHzDZIyrdDWVCddM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/RM-165419-yuca-french-fries-ddmfs-step3-3x4-13183-ac3b1ce9b8894247b83d25ae5a5eee4e.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/165419/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat oil in a deep fryer to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Working in batches, fry yuca in hot oil until golden brown and crispy, about 5 minutes. Remove with a slotted spoon and drain in a paper towel-lined bowl.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/k_3q7GN-O1vnLL9myEXRFvLJQA4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/RM-165419-yuca-french-fries-ddmfs-step5-3x4-13192-a0ebb4da19224d35b18985050f2a0753.jpg"
      ],
